  "lineage": "Working-class urban vernacular music across the Arab world, crystallizing in Cairo's Ahmed Adaweyah cassettes of the early 1970s and paralleled in Baghdad, Amman and the Gulf — fast baladi and maqsum 4/4 patterns at 110-140 BPM on tabla baladi and riq, accordion or organ playing quarter-tone maqam lines, blaring mizmar or keyboard leads, and a hoarse ad-libbing voice trading colloquial couplets with a shouting crowd chorus.",
